<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sino-French War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tonkin War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sino-French War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a> from August 1884 to April 1885 over control of Tonkin in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. France destroyed the Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> and fought in Tonkin and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>, but a reverse at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lang-son">Lạng Sơn</a> in March 1885 brought down <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-ferry">Jules Ferry</a>'s government. The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianjin">Tientsin</a> of June 1885 ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s claims and confirmed the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over Vietnam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-french-war.jpg" alt="Sino-French War" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SinoFrenchWar1884-1885.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
